00:27:04,741 --> 00:27:07,740
So here's Mrs. Larson's, one of her slippers.

351
00:27:07,741 --> 00:27:09,740
I don't know where the other one is.

352
00:27:09,741 --> 00:27:14,740
Okay, here we have all of the letters off the Golden Nugget high rise sign

353
00:27:14,741 --> 00:27:16,740
off of the roof of the Golden Nugget.

354
00:27:16,741 --> 00:27:21,140
To get them down, we have to cut them up into pieces so we can fit them on the trailer.

355
00:27:21,280 --> 00:27:24,160
But somewhere in here, everything spells golden nugget.

356
00:27:24,500 --> 00:27:26,300
We're saving them. We're not throwing them away.

357
00:27:30,180 --> 00:27:33,260
Here in Las Vegas, history belongs to the next landlord.

358
00:27:34,500 --> 00:27:38,740
The town's story is written in the sky on a thousand flashing facades,

359
00:27:39,600 --> 00:27:41,700
mesmerizing signs in the desert.

360
00:27:43,400 --> 00:27:46,140
Perhaps that's the way it goes with all remarkable visions.

361
00:27:46,740 --> 00:27:49,280
The seduction is a burst of illumination.

362
00:27:50,280 --> 00:27:53,240
Their power lies in their lingering hold on our memory.

363
00:28:06,240 --> 00:28:09,300
I wonder if Bugsy Siegel knew where he started here.

364
00:28:10,420 --> 00:28:14,120
It's always been a mecca of show business,

365
00:28:14,121 --> 00:28:17,480
and years ago, of course, it was even more personal

366
00:28:17,481 --> 00:28:21,900
because you had, most of the hotels had individual stars.

367
00:28:23,520 --> 00:28:26,440
Bugsy actually started the modern Las Vegas showroom

