00:28:36,860 --> 00:28:38,220
They had the individual stars.

372
00:28:38,620 --> 00:28:40,940
But so did the Sands. The Sands had the Rat Pack.

373
00:28:40,941 --> 00:28:44,480
They were legendary in this town.

374
00:28:45,140 --> 00:28:49,380
And I believe what made Las Vegas different, what made it great,

375
00:28:50,160 --> 00:28:54,700
people could go from theater to theater to theater,

376
00:28:54,940 --> 00:28:56,680
nightclub to nightclub to nightclub,

377
00:28:56,820 --> 00:28:59,140
and see as many different acts as they wanted to.

378
00:29:04,380 --> 00:29:08,520
It's a Las Vegas tradition that when the sun goes down, the stars come out.

379
00:29:08,521 --> 00:29:18,480
A close proximity to Hollywood and the town's glittering image helped Vegas showrooms develop a reputation as the ultimate venue for performers.

380
00:29:23,880 --> 00:29:28,080
Entertainment royalty made Las Vegas their home away from home.

381
00:29:31,040 --> 00:29:38,040
Kings decided the desert town was the perfect location for their castles, and they presided over a glittering court.

382
00:29:38,520 --> 00:29:46,200
The stage spectaculars tested the bounds of glitter, glamour, and good taste,

383
00:29:46,520 --> 00:29:50,180
and gave rise to the most enduring of Las Vegas' icons,

384
00:29:51,200 --> 00:29:57,780
the showgirl, a scintillating mix of Wild West saloon gal and French can-can dancer.

385
00:29:59,480 --> 00:30:05,820
In 1957, when the Dunes Hotel dared to be the first to import a classic topless review from Paris,

386
00:30:06,540 --> 00:30:09,160
The local Catholic bishop may have called for censorship,

387
00:30:09,740 --> 00:30:12,260
but everyone else called for reservations.

388
00:30:13,880 --> 00:30:18,360
The show was a sellout and helped Vegas earn the nickname Sin City.

389
00:30:18,980 --> 00:30:21,920
It wasn't really sinful. It was grown up.

390
00:30:23,380 --> 00:30:26,420
Today, the stage extravaganzas are no less spectacular,

391
00:30:26,960 --> 00:30:30,320
but they're designed for a broader family audience.

392
00:30:30,321 --> 00:30:39,160
while these spectacles have taken over many of the big showrooms the headliners are still there

393
00:30:39,161 --> 00:30:43,440
offering audiences a more intimate spontaneous experience

394
00:30:43,441 --> 00:30:51,220
i feel that i'm here to meet the people greet the people and entertain the people and give

395
00:30:51,221 --> 00:30:58,340
them a good time in a very simple quiet atmosphere that's still fun in 1993 debbie reynolds bought

396
00:30:58,341 --> 00:31:04,420
the paddle wheel hotel gave it a facelift and created a new vegas phenomenon based on a

397
00:31:04,421 --> 00:31:12,020
traditional idea less is more well i really felt it took a lot of courage to do this because as a

