00:31:12,021 --> 00:31:18,900
performer only and as a woman to come in here and buy a small hotel and hope it's a success

399
00:31:18,901 --> 00:31:22,420
but i never had a dream this big so this is way beyond my dreams

400
00:31:22,421 --> 00:31:31,740
We have a Friday Saturdays a late night show people can come and just hang out sit and visit and we have jazz and jokes and

401
00:31:32,180 --> 00:31:40,140
Lots of comics drop in and singers and fellow performers come by and Tony Bennett was in one night and Leslie Elgums and lots of different folks drop by

402
00:31:40,620 --> 00:31:44,720
So this is really going back to the 50s and the 60s month this concept

403
00:31:44,721 --> 00:31:49,600
Las Vegas has become a big town since Bugsy's day.

404
00:31:50,060 --> 00:31:59,280
So big that there's plenty of room for the wild reviews, the lounge acts, the magicians, and of course the timeless stars.

405
00:32:02,800 --> 00:32:09,600
And I will be here and I'll stay here until I drop dead and then I'll have myself stuffed like Trigger and I'll put me in the museum.

406
00:32:14,720 --> 00:32:26,720
Las Vegas' favorite color has always been green.

407
00:32:26,721 --> 00:32:30,280
Back in the 1950s, it certainly wasn't black.

408
00:32:30,281 --> 00:32:34,880
Back then, black people were not allowed to play in the casinos, were not allowed to stay

409
00:32:34,881 --> 00:32:36,880
in the hotels.

410
00:32:36,881 --> 00:32:45,340
Thus spawned the Moulin Rouge so that they would have a nice facility to live in and gamble.

411
00:32:47,080 --> 00:32:54,520
In 1955, the Moulin Rouge represented a radical departure from the racially divided status quo in Las Vegas.

412
00:32:55,380 --> 00:33:02,380
Here was a resort hotel, itself segregated on the edge of town, which would accept black patrons.

413
00:33:02,381 --> 00:33:08,600
even though the blacks could perform on the strip but they were not allowed to sit at the bar and

