00:33:08,601 --> 00:33:16,340
have a drink so thus they had to come over here in order to do that sammy davis jr was one of las

415
00:33:16,341 --> 00:33:23,940
vegas's biggest attractions in 1955 a full-fledged member of frank sinatra's infamous superstar rat

416
00:33:23,941 --> 00:33:31,200
pack and a frequent guest artist at the moulin rouge sammy did a lot of jam sessions here i don't

417
00:33:31,201 --> 00:33:34,500
I don't think Sammy officially worked here at the Moulin Rouge.

418
00:33:34,501 --> 00:33:39,700
He was appearing in Las Vegas and that was the year that he became a really big star in 1955.

419
00:33:39,701 --> 00:33:42,960
He and his dad and his uncle.

420
00:33:42,961 --> 00:33:46,960
And they frequented over here all the time because that was the only place they could go.

421
00:33:46,961 --> 00:33:53,640
Davis's professional accomplishments made his experience with segregation an uneasy issue.

422
00:33:53,641 --> 00:33:56,640
You're out of your damn mind.

423
00:33:56,641 --> 00:34:01,640
You know you shouldn't sing the leader song, boy.

424
00:34:03,520 --> 00:34:04,840
Damn fool.

425
00:34:06,960 --> 00:34:08,380
What do you want to do about it?

426
00:34:08,381 --> 00:34:09,960
In 1960, they had a meeting.

427
00:34:09,961 --> 00:34:13,020
The city fathers and local NAACP leaders

428
00:34:13,021 --> 00:34:17,760
and the hotel owners all met and signed a consent decree

429
00:34:17,761 --> 00:34:21,900
and agreed to let blacks patronize their facilities.

